 {"file_name": "03.png", "id": "884131511361956", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499314659_884131514695289_5808890142641071213_n.png?_nc_cat=107&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=KL4t0xR36EUQ7kNvwGvqlIv&_nc_oc=AdqLzgj6Ls9DqFrCU37xjkaU0DwBK_hCcD_8ebk0KL8pC1k9NWMFCB8HqsbYHslR0vs&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQXT6DyIlCEX2SruwGAGYV8WGyC1MiUdNDdnwqRGpgvV-g&oe=6B104959"}, {"file_name": "04.png", "id": "2073705526623799", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499313063_2073705529957132_5967704642211820566_n.png?_nc_cat=107&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=w4jTonAyrW0Q7kNvwGQiVv3&_nc_oc=AdpQw0iFa-ykVCO2erOwukT08yHWN4V0DwXaSbWIBXYv6Eaql7DVEic5Q9e5wcznXws&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQXEg8bYVMAYAKKowTk2fjR9Ut-r_oA32t94eUi5vHMSBg&oe=6B106625"}, {"file_name": "05.png", "id": "1110048894841244", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/595119480_1110048898174577_7636723964820635014_n.png?_nc_cat=104&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=-URqvdQ1oFkQ7kNvwGvvghZ&_nc_oc=AdoaDAgs9PrUghKQLS3qy60AQabTMUSSWq9MZfQ7urA2fvSs0aco2AIYsYov4DV1oKw&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQWKQhEHRKr_UOKBIUD507mD1OvOVpdrp5Y20BkjoZ-P0Q&oe=6B10644E"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Immuch360", "keywords": ["360", "VR180", "3D", "splat", "NAS"], "long_description": "Your media. Any screen. Every perspective.\n\nPress 360\u00b0 and a 360\u00b0 photo or video surrounds you. 3D files are in true 3D, VR180 fills a half sphere, an Apple spatial photo floats in front of you, and flat photos and videos play in the window or on a big screen you move.\n\nOn Meta Quest 3 and 3S: Gaussian splats (.ply, .spz) open around you from your folders and shares, including the scenes Immuch360 makes on a computer, or as splat photos of your Immich timeline, where Save to Immich keeps them. AI relief shows a flat photo in 3D. 3D scenes and 360\u00b0 panoramas made on a computer open around you, and each view says what AI made.\n\nKiosk mode: the headset opens your 360\u00b0 film for visitors each time it is put on.\n\nSign in with your phone: type the headset's code in Immuch360 on the phone.\n\nYour drone: an Android phone on a DJI RC-N3 remote relays its live video, to watch only.\n\nYour files where they are: the headset, SMB, WebDAV and DLNA shares, a phone or computer at home, Plex Media Server, your Immich server. Raw Insta360, GoPro MAX and DJI Osmo 360 files are stitched in the headset.\n\nFree and open source (GNU AGPL v3), no ads, no analytics. Gaussian splats use a part of the Meta Spatial SDK that Meta neither supports nor warrants: any defect is Immuch360's own.\n\nImmuch360 is an unofficial fork of the Immich mobile app, not affiliated with nor endorsed by Immich, FUTO, Plex, Meta, Apple, Google, Insta360, GoPro or DJI.", "short_description": "Your photos and videos all around you: 360\u00b0, VR180 and true 3D, panoramas, and flat ones too, played in place from the headset, a NAS, Plex Media Server, a phone or a computer at home, or your Immich server. Films pick up where you stopped. On Meta Quest 3 and 3S: Gaussian splats from your files or your Immich timeline, Save to Immich, the splat scenes, 3D scenes and 360\u00b0 panoramas Immuch360 makes on a computer, and AI relief. Free and open source, no account."}, {"images": {"nodes": []}, "id": "3445897889133246", "locale": "fr_FR", "screenshots": [], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Immuch360", "keywords": ["360", "VR180", "3D", "splat", "NAS"], "long_description": "Vos m\u00e9dias. Tous les \u00e9crans. Tous les points de vue.\n\nAppuyez sur 360\u00b0 et la photo ou la vid\u00e9o vous entoure. La 3D est en vraie 3D, le VR180 remplit une demi-sph\u00e8re, une photo spatiale Apple flotte devant vous, le reste se lit en fen\u00eatre ou sur un grand \u00e9cran mobile.\n\nSur Meta Quest 3 et 3S : splats gaussiens (.ply, .spz) de vos dossiers et partages, dont les sc\u00e8nes faites sur ordinateur, ou en photos splat de votre chronologie Immich, o\u00f9 Enregistrer dans Immich les garde. Le relief IA met en 3D une photo \u00e0 plat. Sc\u00e8nes 3D et panoramas 360\u00b0 faits sur ordinateur vous entourent, et chaque vue dit ce que l'IA a fait.\n\nMode kiosque : le casque ouvre votre film 360\u00b0 aux visiteurs d\u00e8s qu'on le met.\n\nConnexion : tapez le code du casque dans Immuch360 sur le t\u00e9l\u00e9phone.\n\nVotre drone : un t\u00e9l\u00e9phone Android sur une radiocommande DJI RC-N3 relaie son image en direct.\n\nVos fichiers sur place : le casque, partages SMB, WebDAV et DLNA, t\u00e9l\u00e9phone ou PC de la maison, Plex Media Server ou serveur Immich. Fichiers bruts Insta360, GoPro MAX et DJI Osmo 360 assembl\u00e9s.\n\nLibre, gratuit (GNU AGPL v3), sans publicit\u00e9 ni statistiques. Les splats gaussiens utilisent une partie du Meta Spatial SDK que Meta ne prend pas en charge et ne garantit pas : tout d\u00e9faut rel\u00e8ve d'Immuch360 seul.\n\nImmuch360, fork non officiel de l'appli mobile Immich, n'est ni affili\u00e9 \u00e0 Immich, FUTO, Plex, Meta, Apple, Google, Insta360, GoPro ou DJI, ni approuv\u00e9 par eux.", "short_description": "Vos photos et vid\u00e9os tout autour de vous : 360\u00b0, VR180, vraie 3D, panoramas et photos \u00e0 plat, lues sur place depuis le casque, un NAS, Plex Media Server, un t\u00e9l\u00e9phone ou ordinateur de la maison, ou votre serveur Immich. Les films reprennent o\u00f9 vous les avez laiss\u00e9s. Sur Meta Quest 3 et 3S : splats gaussiens de vos fichiers ou de votre chronologie Immich, Enregistrer dans Immich, sc\u00e8nes splat, sc\u00e8nes 3D et panoramas 360\u00b0 faits sur ordinateur, relief IA. Libre, sans compte."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://github.com/freeKC/Immuch360/blo